From 9d6a81b34fda33188762de8295da90ab58272861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] NEXUS engine: host-memory cap for the texture cache on
 Linux

Common::GetSystemCommitRoom returned no value outside Windows, so the
texture cache's host-memory cap (HostCriticalMemory) was off on Linux.
On a 16 GB shared-memory handheld a Switch 2 game's 12 GiB of guest
memory and the texture cache then compete for the same RAM and the OOM
killer ends the session instead of the cache collecting.

Linux now reports MemAvailable + SwapFree (heuristic overcommit, the
default and SteamOS's mode) or CommitLimit - Committed_AS (strict
overcommit, matching Windows' commit semantics). Parsing is a small
header so it is unit-tested on every platform.

Idea credited to Fritchii's fixed texture-cache ceiling; this feeds the
host's real room into the cap Lichii already has instead of a constant.
Not measured on a handheld.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
(cherry picked from commit e86bf7b54261040d94a9738274985ccd999cf01a)
